First create image using dockerfile and app.js
   ---check these are running or not 
        --- Docker installer
        --- running docker desktop
        --- docker registry
        --- kubernetes version
        --- minikube status
Either you can use clone git Repositry or use directly
## Create a file called 'app.js'
markdown
```javascript
// app.js
const http = require("http");

http.createServer((req, res) => {
  res.end("Multi-stage Dockerfile practice");
}).listen(3000);

## create a file called dockerfile
dockerfile
# Stage 1: Build
FROM node:18-alpine AS builder
WORKDIR /app
COPY package.json .
RUN npm install
COPY . .

# Stage 2: Runtime
FROM node:18-alpine
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=builder /app /app
EXPOSE 3000
CMD ["node", "app.js"]

docker build -t lokesh815/my-first-docker-image1:latest .

docker run -it lokesh815/my-first-docker-image

login to docker registry

docker push lokesh815/my-first-docker-image:latest

After successfully create image check for kubernetes 

kubectl version

Next minikube status
minikube start( it runs in docker desktop driver if you don't have any driver like virtualbox..)
if you have virtualbox
minkube start --memory=4096 --driver=virtualbox

## create deployment.yml file 
vim deployment.yml
yml 
  apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: demo-deployment
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: demo-app
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: demo-app
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: demo-container
        image: lokesh815/my-first-docker-image1:latest
        ports:
        - containerPort: 3000


